---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  PRODUCT_NAME,
  CURRENT_LINE,
  V1_LINE,
  V2_LINE,
  VENDOR,
  COMPANY_KVK,
  SOURCE_PUBLICATION,
  LICENSING_TERMS_URL,
} from '../data/product-facts.mjs';

// OWNER: set the effective date at GA. The "Version YYYY-MM" literal in the
// markup below must stay in lockstep with TERMS_VERSION_WEB in
// src/pages/buy/index.astro — test/sync/terms-version-sync.test.ts guards it.
const PRODUCT = `${PRODUCT_NAME} ${CURRENT_LINE}`;
const LICENSE = SOURCE_PUBLICATION.license;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service — mod_pagespeed"
  description={`Terms of service for modpagespeed.com, the free package repository, the subscriber repository and support subscriptions. The software itself is ${LICENSE}-licensed. ${VENDOR}, the Netherlands.`}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-text-body">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-text-annotation">
      Effective date: September 2026 &middot; Version 2026-09
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-text-muted">
      These terms are written in plain language. If something is unclear, email
      <a
        href="mailto:info@we-amp.com"
        class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">info@we-amp.com</a
      > and we will clarify.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 space-y-10">
      <!-- Scope -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">What these terms cover</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          {VENDOR}, a company registered in the Netherlands (KvK
          <span class="font-mono">{COMPANY_KVK}</span>) and based in Castricum, operates
          modpagespeed.com and the services around {PRODUCT} and its predecessor lines. These terms govern
          your use of:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>the websites we operate for the product, and the tools on them;</li>
          <li>
            the free standard package repository at
            <code class="font-mono text-sm">packages.modpagespeed.com</code>;
          </li>
          <li>the subscriber repository through which we deliver hardened attested builds; and</li>
          <li>support subscriptions.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          They apply from the moment you use one of these services. If you use them on behalf of a
          company or other organization, you confirm that you are authorized to bind it, and
          &ldquo;you&rdquo; means that organization. These terms do not govern the software itself
          &mdash; the next section explains what does.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Software license -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">The software license</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software &mdash; {PRODUCT}, and the predecessor lines mod_pagespeed {V1_LINE} and ModPageSpeed
          {V2_LINE} &mdash; is licensed under the {LICENSE}. That license, not these terms, governs
          your rights to install, run, copy, modify and redistribute the software. It applies to
          every artifact we publish, including the hardened attested builds: an artifact you obtain
          through a subscription carries the same license as a standard package.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          Nothing in these terms narrows the rights the {LICENSE} grants you. Where these terms and that
          license appear to conflict about the software, the license prevails. The license text is on
          the
          <a href="/license/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
            >license page</a
          > and ships with every package. Third-party components inside the software remain under their
          own licenses, listed in the packages.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          mod_pagespeed is an open-source project originally developed at Google. {PRODUCT} is developed
          by {VENDOR} and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Free standard channel -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">The free standard packages</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The standard signed packages at
          <code class="font-mono text-sm">packages.modpagespeed.com</code> are free of charge for everyone,
          for any number of servers, in development and in production. The repository is public: no account
          is needed and none is offered, and we do not ask you to register before you install. Every package
          is signed so you can verify what you install.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          We run the standard repository on a best-effort basis. We aim to keep it available and to
          keep its packages current, but we do not promise uptime, a release schedule, or continued
          publication of any particular package, and we may reorganize the repository with
          reasonable notice on this site. The software in it comes with the warranty terms of the {
            LICENSE
          }
          &mdash; that is, as-is, without warranty &mdash; and these terms add none.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Subscriptions -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Subscriptions</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">We sell two things:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Support subscriptions.</strong> Support from the people who build the product: a direct
            channel, agreed response times for configuration, upgrade and incident questions, and SLA-backed
            delivery of security updates. The scope, response times and contact channel of your subscription
            are set out in your order.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Hardened attested builds.</strong> Builds of the same code the standard packages are
            built from, produced through a hardened build pipeline and shipped with a signed software
            bill of materials (SBOM) and build provenance, delivered through a subscriber repository.
            They differ from the standard packages in how they are built and attested, never in features.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What a subscription grants.</strong> For its term, a subscription gives you access to
          the subscriber repository and the builds in it, the support services in your order, and the
          SBOM and provenance documents for the builds you obtain. Access to the subscriber repository
          is for your organization: do not share it outside your organization or use it to mirror the
          repository for others. You may deploy the builds you obtain on as many of your own systems as
          you like, and you may redistribute them under the {LICENSE} &mdash; the restriction is on access
          to the repository, not on the artifacts.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What a subscription does not do.</strong> A subscription covers access to the subscriber
          repository and to support. The software itself is the same for everyone and behaves the same
          with or without one. A subscription grants no rights in the software beyond the {LICENSE},
          and it does not make us responsible for your deployment (see
          <em>Your responsibilities</em>).
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Ordering, term and cancellation.</strong> Pricing is published on the
          <a href="/pricing/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
            >pricing page</a
          > when available; until then, subscriptions are arranged directly with us. Subscriptions run
          for the term stated in your order and renew as stated there. You can cancel at any time; cancellation
          takes effect at the end of the current term. Where a merchant of record handles payment, its
          terms apply to the payment and to refunds. Where your order or a subscription agreement states
          something different from these terms, the order or agreement prevails for that subscription;
          the
          <a
            href={LICENSING_TERMS_URL}
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">We-Amp support terms</a
          > apply alongside these terms.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Consumers (EU/EEA).</strong> If you are a consumer, you have a 14-day right of withdrawal
          from a subscription under Directive 2011/83/EU. If you ask us to begin performing immediately
          and acknowledge that you thereby lose that right, it ends when performance begins. Your mandatory
          statutory rights are unaffected.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Ending a subscription.</strong> We may suspend or end a subscription if you materially
          breach these terms and do not remedy the breach within 14 days of our written notice; sharing
          subscriber repository access outside your organization ends it immediately. When a subscription
          ends, for whatever reason, access to the subscriber repository and to support ends with it.
          Your right to keep using, modifying and redistributing every artifact you already obtained does
          not end: those artifacts are licensed under the {LICENSE}, and nothing we do under these
          terms revokes that license.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Acceptable use -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Acceptable use of the services</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          When using our websites, tools and repositories, you may not:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>
            overload, load-test, scrape or benchmark our websites, demo tools or repositories
            without our written permission;
          </li>
          <li>
            circumvent access controls on the subscriber repository, or share its access details
            outside your organization;
          </li>
          <li>submit sites you have no right to test to the analysis tools on this site;</li>
          <li>use the services to attack, disrupt or overload third-party systems; or</li>
          <li>misrepresent the origin or attestation of a build.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          These rules are about the services. They do not restrict what you do with the software,
          which is governed by the {LICENSE}.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Your responsibilities -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Your responsibilities</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software runs inline in your web stack and rewrites your live HTTP responses. Before
          you deploy it to production &mdash; and before you deploy any new version, configuration
          change or filter to production &mdash; you agree to:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc list-inside text-text-muted space-y-1">
          <li>
            <strong>Test it first</strong> in a staging or non-production environment that mirrors your
            production setup, and confirm it behaves as you expect.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep your own backups</strong> and a tested <strong>rollback plan</strong>, so
            you can disable the software or revert your configuration quickly.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Configure the software correctly</strong> for your environment and keep it reasonably
            up to date.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          You are responsible for your server configuration, your content and your deployment
          decisions. Roll out gradually &mdash; for example, to a subset of traffic &mdash; and
          monitor before a full rollout. Loss that results from deploying without testing, from
          misconfiguration, or from missing backups or a rollback plan is attributable to you and
          reduces our liability accordingly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Warranty and liability -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Warranty and liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>The software.</strong> The software is provided under the {LICENSE} on an &ldquo;as
          is&rdquo; basis, without warranties or conditions of any kind. The license says so, and these
          terms add no warranty on top of it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>The services.</strong> We perform support with reasonable skill and care, within the
          response times in your order. We do not warrant that support will resolve every issue, or that
          a hardened build is free of defects or vulnerabilities: the attestation describes how a build
          was produced and what went into it, not that it is defect-free. The free services are provided
          as-is.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          The rest of this section applies to business customers. If you are a consumer in the
          EU/EEA, see <em>Consumers</em> at the end of this section &mdash; these limits do not take away
          your statutory rights.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss.</strong> This includes lost profits,
          lost revenue, lost or corrupted data, business interruption, loss of goodwill, and claims made
          against you by third parties &mdash; whether or not we were told such loss was possible.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Cap on our liability.</strong> For all other loss, our total liability to you in connection
          with these terms, for all claims combined, is limited to the greater of (a) the total fees you
          paid us in the 12 months immediately before the first event giving rise to a claim, or (b) &euro;500.
          This is an aggregate cap across all claims, not a cap per claim. It applies regardless of the
          legal basis of the claim &mdash; contract, tort (<em>onrechtmatige daad</em>), statute or
          otherwise.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Time limit for claims.</strong> You must tell us about a claim in writing within 30
          days of discovering the issue, and in any event within 12 months of the event that caused it.
          After that, the claim lapses.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-text-muted">
          <strong>What we never limit or exclude.</strong> Nothing in these terms limits or excludes our
          liability for fraud; for intent (<em>opzet</em>) or deliberate recklessness (<em
            >bewuste roekeloosheid</em
          >) of {VENDOR} or of the persons charged with its management or direction; for death or personal
          injury caused by our negligence; or for anything else that cannot be limited or excluded under
          applicable law.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          <strong>Consumers (EU/EEA).</strong> If you are a consumer, nothing in this section reduces
          your mandatory statutory rights, including your legal warranty rights for digital content and
          services and your 14-day right of withdrawal. None of the limits in this section applies to
          you to the extent it would conflict with those rights.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Force majeure -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Circumstances beyond our control</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We are not responsible for a failure or delay in operating our websites, repositories or
          support when it is caused by events beyond our reasonable control &mdash; for example,
          outages at our hosting, network or payment providers, internet or infrastructure failures,
          security incidents, natural events, or government action. While such circumstances
          continue, our affected obligations are suspended rather than breached. If they continue
          for more than 60 days, either you or we may end an affected subscription, and we will
          refund any fees you have paid for the unused period.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Data -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Data</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          The software runs on your servers, sends nothing to us, and never processes your
          visitors&rsquo; data on our behalf. What our websites and services do with personal data,
          and what the software does and does not send, is described in our
          <a href="/privacy/" class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline"
            >privacy notice</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Changes -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          We may update these terms as the product, the law or our processes change. Changes that
          affect a subscription are announced to subscribers by email at least 30 days before they
          take effect; if you do not agree, you may cancel before that date and we will refund any
          prepaid fees for the remaining term. Changes to the terms for the free services take
          effect when published here. The version and date at the top of this page are updated with
          every change.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Governing law -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Governing law and venue</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Netherlands. Disputes arising from these terms
          or from your use of the services are submitted to the competent court in Amsterdam, the
          Netherlands. If you are a consumer, you keep the right to bring a claim before the court
          that the law designates for you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Severability and survival -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Severability and survival</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          If a provision of these terms (or part of one) is found invalid or unenforceable, it is
          reduced to the minimum extent needed to make it enforceable or, if it cannot be, severed;
          the remaining provisions stay in full force. <em>The software license</em>,
          <em>Warranty and liability</em>, <em>Acceptable use of the services</em> and
          <em>Governing law and venue</em> continue to apply after a subscription or these terms end.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Contact -->
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-text-body">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-text-muted">
          Questions about these terms go to
          <a
            href="mailto:info@we-amp.com"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">info@we-amp.com</a
          >. Questions about a subscription go to
          <a
            href="mailto:license@we-amp.com"
            class="text-interactive hover:text-interactive-hover underline">license@we-amp.com</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
